name 'thinking-critically-about-ai-postassessment-q13_2026-pilot_2026'

question 'A student overshares details about their daily routine on a public app. They say, "It\'s fine — none of this is sensitive information." Which response most accurately challenges their assumption?'

wrong 'They are right. Public information about daily routines cannot be used to identify anyone.'
wrong 'They are wrong only if they also share their phone number or home address.'
right 'Even information that seems harmless individually — like a daily schedule or neighborhood — can be combined by AI systems to infer sensitive patterns about a person\'s life, location, and habits.'
wrong 'They are right as long as their social media privacy settings are turned on.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

